{title: Bear Your Disgrace}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 16:15–63}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Am] | [Am] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
You trusted in [Dm]your beauty and [E]played [Am]the whore
Lavished your favors on every passerby
Took garments and made gaudy [Dm]shrines for them
Used my gold and silver to make [E]male images
Set my oil and incense [Am]before these idols
Sacrificed your sons and daughters to the fire
Did not remember the days [Dm]of your youth
When you were naked and kicking [E]in your blood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hear the word of the Lord regarding you
[Am]I will gather all your lovers against you
Strip you na[Fmaj7]ked before them in the square
They will tear down [Dm]your mound and lofty shrines
Stone you and [E]cut you with their swords
I will spend [Am]my wrath and my jealousy
Then I [Fmaj7]will be calm and no longer an[Dm]gry
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]You built a mound at the [Am]head of every street
Degraded your beauty for every passerby
Played the whore with the Egyp[Dm]tians and Assyria
Multiplied your whorings with Chal[E]dea too
You scorned payment like a brazen [Am]prostitute
Opposite of women who solicited love
You are truly your mother's daughter in[Dm]deed
Who despised her husband and [E]her children
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hear the word of the Lord regarding you
I will gather all [Am]your lovers against you
Strip you naked be[Fmaj7]fore them in the square
They will tear down your [Dm]mound and lofty shrines
Stone you and [E]cut you with their swords
I will spend [Am]my wrath and my jealousy
Then I will be [Fmaj7]calm and no longer angry
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Your old[Dm]er [E]sister Samaria lived to the [Am]north
Your younger sister Sodom lived to the south
You copied their abominations and [Dm]ways
Became more corrupt in all your deeds
[E]Sodom was arrogant and over[Am]fed with ease
Did not help the poor and the needy
Samaria did not commit half [Dm]your sins
You made your sisters look right[E]eous by contrast
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will restore the fortunes of them [Am]all
So you may bear your disgrace and be [Dm]ashamed
They will return to [E]their former state
[Am]And you will be a consolation [Dm]to [E]them
{end_of_verse}

